AegisTrace is a project of Nexus Security & AI Lab. It is a laboratory-grade incident investigation tool. It has not been independently audited. It ships with
synthetic demonstration data only, and its response actions are simulated. See docs/THREAT-MODEL.md before using it
with real data.

Third-party software
--------------------
This project depends on open-source packages, all under permissive licenses compatible with Apache-2.0:
  - npm (api, web): MIT, ISC and BSD-3-Clause packages (for example Express, zod, React, jose, pg, redis).
  - Python (analytics): FastAPI and Pydantic (MIT), Starlette and Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause).
  - Optional components used only for testing/deployment and not redistributed here: PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL License),
    Redis, Caddy (Apache-2.0), Dex (Apache-2.0).
Each package keeps its own license; consult the package metadata for the exact terms.
